From c866c1c8d7f43f338e74603e96250b128d7428b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] docs: document plugin signing, grants and in-process
 isolation

The plugin guide, SECURITY.md, the README and the module mapping still
described the old supply chain: HMAC signing, a restricted RPC host
that never existed and permissions taken from the manifest. Describe
what the code does now: Ed25519 signatures verified at registration
against the trusted keys of the plugin policy file, permissions granted
by the administrator, module:Class entrypoints loaded in-process and no
process isolation.

Record the missing restricted RPC host as deviation D3 in the module
mapping and as the implementation status of ADR-006, list the changes
in the 1.1.0 changelog with the breaking ones marked, and state that
the control plane application does not build a PluginManager yet, so
there is no environment variable to configure.
